  "worked_solution": "To calculate the average value of the acceleration on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{a}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}a(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{4-1}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 8)-(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{14}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{9}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average acceleration is $\\frac{14}{9}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$",
